msgstr "Google Sans Flex (ship's own)"

msgid "System font"
msgstr "The system's lettering"

msgid "Size"
msgstr "Size o' the ship"

msgid ""
"Automatic is Compact in a narrow window. Ctrl+minus and Ctrl+plus change it, Ctrl+0 goes back to "
"Automatic."
msgstr ""
"Automatic be a Dinghy in a narrow window. Ctrl+minus an' Ctrl+plus change it, Ctrl+0 sails back "
"to Automatic."

msgid "Window buttons"
msgstr "Porthole buttons"

msgid "Minimize, maximize and close at the top. Off: use your desktop's own keys or menu."
msgstr "Stow, hoist an' scuttle up top. Off: use yer desktop's own keys or menu."

msgid "Reduce motion"
msgstr "Calm the seas"

msgid "Turns off shape morphs, sliding panels and the color cross-fade."
msgstr "Stops the shape-shiftin', slidin' panels and the color fades."

msgid "Night mode and sleep"
msgstr "Night watch an' slumber"

msgid "Dim the LEDs at night, and turn them off while the PC sleeps."
msgstr "Dim the lanterns at night, and douse 'em while the ship sleeps."

msgid "From"
msgstr "From"

msgid "to"
msgstr "to"

msgid "brightness at most"
msgstr "brightness no more than"

msgid "Times are 24 hour, like 23:00. The window can cross midnight."
msgstr "Ship's time be 24 hour, like 23:00. The watch can sail past midnight."

msgid "Turn the LEDs off while the PC sleeps"
msgstr "Douse the lanterns while the ship sleeps"

msgid "Flashing LEDs for desktop notifications has its own tab now."
msgstr "Flashin' lanterns fer messages has its own tab now."

msgid "Open"
msgstr "Open"

msgid "Setups and backups"
msgstr "Charts an' buried treasure"

msgid ""
"Save everything (devices, zones, layout, night mode, calibration, your colors for each wallpaper "
"and your saved colors) under a name, and load it again later."
msgstr ""
"Bury everything (cargo, zones, the treasure map, night watch, calibration, yer colors fer each "
"wallpaper an' yer chest o' colors) under a name, and dig it up again later."

msgid "Setup"
msgstr "Chart"

msgid "No setups yet"
msgstr "No charts yet"

msgid "Save current as…"
msgstr "Bury what we have as…"

msgid "Load"
msgstr "Dig up"

msgid "Export"
msgstr "Send by bottle"

msgid "Import"
msgstr "Fish a bottle out"

msgid "Delete"
msgstr "Make 'em walk the plank"

msgid "Automatic backups"
msgstr "Automatic buried treasure"

msgid "No backups yet"
msgstr "Nothin' buried yet"

msgid "Loading a setup first saves what you have now as an automatic backup, so you can always go back."
msgstr "Diggin' up a chart first buries what ye have now, so ye can always sail back."

msgid "Color calibration"
msgstr "Color calibration"

msgid ""
"Profiles that correct colors for your kind of LED strip. Pick one per zone with Color correction:"
" Calibrated on the Devices tab."
msgstr ""
"Profiles that correct colors fer yer kind o' strip. Pick one per zone with Color correction: "
"Calibrated on the Cargo deck."

msgid "Profile"
msgstr "Profile"

msgid "Edit"
msgstr "Tinker"

msgid "Add"
msgstr "Add"

msgid "Color extraction"
msgstr "Plunderin' colors"

msgid "How Iridia picks colors from your wallpaper."
msgstr "How Iridia plunders colors from yer wallpaper."

msgid ""
"Automatic (recommended): Caelestia's own colors if Caelestia set the wallpaper, otherwise "
"Material, otherwise Pillow"
msgstr ""
"Automatic (the captain's choice): Caelestia's own colors if Caelestia hung the wallpaper, "
"otherwise Material, otherwise Pillow"

msgid "Material: prominent colors from the image (needs material-color-utilities)"
msgstr "Material: the boldest colors in the picture (needs material-color-utilities)"

msgid "Pillow: median-cut dominant colors, no extra dependencies"
msgstr "Pillow: median-cut colors, no extra cargo needed"

msgid "Reset wallpaper detection cache"
msgstr "Forget how we found the wallpaper"

msgid "Forget all saved wallpaper colors"
msgstr "Throw every wallpaper's picks overboard"

msgid ""
"Once a way of finding your wallpaper works, Iridia remembers it instead of trying every method. "
"Reset this after changing wallpaper tool or shell."
msgstr ""
"Once a way o' findin' yer wallpaper works, Iridia remembers it instead o' tryin' every trick. "
"Reset this after changin' yer wallpaper tool or shell."

msgid "Logging"
msgstr "Captain's log"

msgid "Write a log file"
msgstr "Write in the log book"

msgid "Recent log"
msgstr "Latest log entries"

msgid "The daemon's latest messages. Works even with the log file switched off."
msgstr "The bosun's latest mutterings. Works even with the log book closed."

msgid "Lines"
msgstr "Lines"

msgid "Show"
msgstr "Show"

msgid "Copy"
msgstr "Copy"

msgid "Log copied"
msgstr "Log copied"

msgid "Press Show to load the latest lines."
msgstr "Press Show to read the latest lines."

msgid "New versions of Iridia come from its releases on GitHub."
msgstr "New charts for Iridia come from its releases on GitHub."

msgid "Check now"
msgstr "Check the horizon"

msgid "Update now"
msgstr "Hoist the new sails"

msgid "Skip this version"
msgstr "Let this one sail by"

msgid "What's new"
msgstr "What be new"

msgid ""
"Updating needs no password: the new version installs like the old one, into your home folder. "
"Your settings are backed up first (Settings, Setups and backups)."
msgstr ""
"Updatin' needs no password: the new version lands like the old one, in yer home port. Yer "
"settings be stowed first (Settings, Setups and backups)."

msgid "Checking"
msgstr "Lookout"

msgid "Look for updates when Iridia starts"
msgstr "Look fer new charts when Iridia starts"

msgid "Show a notification when there's a new version"
msgstr "Fire a flare when there be a new version"

msgid "Include test versions"
msgstr "Include test voyages"

msgid ""
"Iridia asks GitHub at most once every few hours, when the daemon or this window starts, and sends"
" nothing about you."
msgstr ""
"Iridia asks GitHub at most once every few hours, when the daemon or this window starts, an' tells"
" 'em nothin' about ye."

msgid "Go back"
msgstr "Sail back"

msgid "The version before the last update is kept, so you can undo an update."
msgstr "The version afore the last update be kept, so ye can undo an update."

