msgstr "That didn't work: see the output below. Nothin' o' yers was changed."

msgid "Monitor brightness"
msgstr "Spyglass brightness"

msgid ""
"Strips with Follow monitor brightness on (under Brightness, on each strip) take their brightness "
"from this monitor."
msgstr ""
"Strips that follow the spyglass (under Brightness, on each strip) take their glow from this one, "
"arr."

msgid "Monitor"
msgstr "Spyglass"

msgid "Look again"
msgstr "Look again, matey"

msgid "Looking for monitors…"
msgstr "Scannin' the horizon for spyglasses…"

msgid "Install ddcutil"
msgstr "Haul in ddcutil"

msgid "Automatic follows the first monitor that answers. A monitor you pick is the only one followed."
msgstr "Automatic follows the first spyglass that answers. Pick one, an' only that one be followed."

msgid "your package manager"
msgstr "yer package manager"

#, python-brace-format
msgid "Install ddcutil with {how}, then press Look again."
msgstr "Haul in ddcutil with {how}, then press Look again, matey."

msgid "ddcutil installed. Looking for monitors…"
msgstr "ddcutil be aboard. Scannin' for spyglasses…"

msgid "Not installed: the password dialog was closed."
msgstr "Not hauled in: ye closed the password scroll."

#, python-brace-format
msgid "Couldn't install ddcutil (the package manager failed). Try it in a terminal: sudo {cmd}"
msgstr "Couldn't haul in ddcutil (the package manager ran aground). Try it in a terminal: sudo {cmd}"

#, python-brace-format
msgid "I2C bus {n}"
msgstr "I2C bus {n}, arr"

msgid "doesn't answer"
msgstr "be silent as the deep"

msgid "Following the screen's backlight."
msgstr "Followin' the screen's lantern."

msgid "the monitor"
msgstr "the spyglass"

#, python-brace-format
msgid "Following {name}, now at {n}%."
msgstr "Followin' {name}, now at {n}%."

#, python-brace-format
msgid "Following {name} once a strip has Follow monitor brightness on."
msgstr "Followin' {name} once a strip follows the spyglass."

msgid ""
"ddcutil isn't installed, so no monitor brightness can be read. Install ddcutil sets it up (it "
"asks for your password), or install the ddcutil package yourself and press Look again."
msgstr ""
"ddcutil ain't aboard, so no spyglass brightness can be read. Haul in ddcutil sets it up (it asks "
"for yer password), or haul in the ddcutil package yerself and press Look again."

msgid ""
"ddcutil finds no monitor. Some docks and adapters don't pass brightness through, and after "
"installing Iridia you may need to log out and in once."
msgstr ""
"ddcutil spies no spyglass. Some docks an' adapters keep the brightness to themselves, an' after "
"installin' Iridia ye may need to go ashore an' back once."

msgid "No monitor answers. Turn DDC/CI on in the monitor's own menu, then press Look again."
msgstr "No spyglass answers. Turn DDC/CI on in the spyglass's own menu, then press Look again, matey."

msgid "This monitor doesn't answer. Turn DDC/CI on in its own menu, or pick another one."
msgstr "This spyglass be silent. Turn DDC/CI on in its own menu, or pick another, arr."

msgid "No monitor brightness to follow."
msgstr "No spyglass brightness to follow."

msgid "Strips that follow it use their Manual brightness meanwhile."
msgstr "Strips that follow it use their By hand brightness till then."

msgid "Lock and idle"
msgstr "Lock an' shore leave"

msgid ""
"Dim or turn off the LEDs when the screen locks or you're away. Strips can stay lit: see "
"Brightness on each strip."
msgstr ""
"Dim or douse the lanterns when the hatch be locked or ye've gone ashore. Strips can stay lit: see"
" Brightness on each strip."

msgid "Keep"
msgstr "Hold fast"

msgid "Dim"
msgstr "Dim"

